{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's perception (obstacle events) and motion (controllable actions). The specification automata enforce safe, coverage-biased exploration: forward/random_walk in clear, conservative recovery on obstacles, and rapid return to exploration. Only one controllable is enabled per state. Recovery uses move_backward or a short turn, with full_rotate reserved for repeated blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plants for modularity.",
    "Specification binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
